            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"God or Jesus Christ as a firm, immovable foundation, ultimate protector, and source of salvation.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Psalm 18:2\",\"Deuteronomy 32:4\",\"1 Corinthians 10:4\",\"Matthew 7:24-27\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The Apostle Peter as the earthly foundation of the Christian Church\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 16:18\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The confession of faith made by Peter regarding Jesus as the Messiah\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 16:18\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A stumbling stone or rock of offense to those who reject the gospel\",\"basis\":[\"Romans 9:33\",\"1 Peter 2:8\",\"Isaiah 8:14\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The overarching symbol of God or Christ as a dependable foundation is universally accepted. The most significant divergence involves Matthew 16:18, where the rock is debated as being Peter himself (traditionally Catholic), his confession of faith (traditionally Protestant), or Christ alone.\"}",
